statement.requirement:
The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the query/response for a the medication list associated with the most recent medication reconciliation event, for example:
- Constrained to the last outpatient encounter, ER visit, discharge from inpatient or extended care encounter;
- Constrained to EHR systems of other providers;
- Constrained to event date/time, organization, practitioner, encounter type.

The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation that the patient is not currently taking a medication and the current status of the medication. Status includes that the medication is:
- Stopped, as directed by clinician;
- Stopped by patient;
- On hold, as directed by clinician;
- On hold by patient.

The system SHALL provide the ability to render reports for printing or export (e.g., using a style sheet) per the preference of the patient - recommended presentation examples include: 
- Grouped by time of day, then alpha sort of generic (+ trade) name of medications with dosages as grouped sections (e.g., list of medications taken once a day in the AM);
- Calendar (grid) week view, with x-axis as day of week and y-axis as time of day;
- Include graphical version options with color pictures of the pills, pill markings;
- Medical Assistant view – alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
- Clinician view – by discipline, grouped by confirm / not taking / update / add, then alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
- Patient-generated medication list (as electronic output) – all fields.
